{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For you have pressed.</b> The meaning is pressed; likewise in \"the wicked have pressed me\" (Psalm 119:51), which is from the root רטה. For if it were from ירט it would be fitting to be like יעטני. And if they are two roots, its parallel is \"a cloak of righteousness—let it cover me\" (Job 29:14), which is on the pattern of \"which You have counseled me,\" like עוטה אור."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:59.152483239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}